    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math a bit intimidating, especially compared to subjects like biology or art. My upper secondary education covered basic algebra and geometry, but I never felt deeply connected to it. I enjoy the logic behind equations, but I don’t see myself as a math person. Still, I appreciate how math underpins real-world problems, like in travel planning or board games.",
